# training-atr-models — asteraix (130.92.59.242)
#
# Copy to .env. The unit reads it with EnvironmentFile=.
#
# IMPORTANT, and new since the split: until 16.09.2026 the gateway and the
# trainer read the SAME .env on one machine. They now read two files on two
# machines, and four values have to agree across them or the handover breaks
# silently. They are marked >>> SHARED <<< below.

# ── the shared secret ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# >>> SHARED <<< with idhefix. Used in both directions now: idhefix presents it
# to this host's /train/* proxy target, and this host presents it to idhefix for
# the promotion gate and for eval/.
ATR_API_KEY=replace-with-a-long-random-shared-secret

# ── where the corpora and the trained weights live ───────────────────────────
# The research share, mounted on BOTH machines. That is what makes the handover
# cheap: the gateway on idhefix reads a path this host wrote, and the 48 job
# records written before the split are already readable here.
#
# !! ONE trainer per job store, ever. JobStore.reconcile marks a running job
# failed when its pid is not alive LOCALLY, on every scheduler tick — so a second
# trainer on another host would declare this host's runs dead, and both would
# grab every queued job (#15). While idhefix's atr-train still runs, point this
# host at its own store (training_folder/jobs-asteraix). At cutover: stop AND
# disable atr-train on idhefix first, then switch to the shared store below.
ATR_TRAIN_JOBS_ROOT=/mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/training_folder/jobs
# >>> SHARED <<< with idhefix — every registration's local_path is an absolute
# path under this directory, and the kraken engine on idhefix opens it as written,
# so the share must be mounted at the same path there. Since serving#138 a path
# that does not exist on idhefix is logged there and a request for the model
# fails naming it; before, resolve_weights took it for a DOI. It must be on the
# same filesystem as ATR_TRAIN_REGISTRY_ROOT below: a registration of weights
# anywhere else fails the job (the default, ~/atr-cache/trained, is local disk).
ATR_TRAIN_TRAINED_ROOT=/mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/training_folder/trained

# ── what must NOT go on the share ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both of these are local *because the share broke them*, not as an optimisation:
#   checkpoints — the trainer saves via temp-file + rename, which is cross-device
#                 on CIFS (training/settings.py:43-50)
#   TMPDIR      — the datasets Arrow cache on the share cost one run 11½ hours
#                 (training/preflight.py:151-175)
# ATR_TRAIN_CHECKPOINT_ROOT defaults to ~/atr-cache/checkpoints; leave it local.
TMPDIR=/home/tobias/atr-cache/tmp

# ── the artefact cache (#109) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local disk, 100 GB budget. Note that it does NOT follow the data: the same
# share gives this host the same ground truth and the same HF cache, but a COLD
# artefact cache — the compile per selection is paid once more here.
# ATR_TRAIN_ARTEFACT_CACHE_ROOT=/home/tobias/atr-cache/artefacts

# ── the model registry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# >>> SHARED <<< — MUST equal ATR_REGISTRY_ROOT in the gateway's .env on idhefix.
# One directory, two directions (serving-atr-inference#138):
#   models.yaml        the gateway PUBLISHES it; this host reads it, and only
#                      kraken does, to resolve a base_model given as a registry id
#   trained/<id>.yaml  this host WRITES one per trained model (#14); the gateway
#                      serves them without a restart
# A mismatch fails no request: models register into a directory the gateway
# never reads, and base models resolve against a file it never publishes. Since
# #14 a job whose registration cannot be written FAILS, naming where the weights
# are — but a wrong directory that happens to exist is written to happily.
# The default in settings.py is already this path; it is repeated here because
# it is one of the values that must agree across the two machines.
ATR_TRAIN_REGISTRY_ROOT=/mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/registry
# The curated file is derived from the root (<root>/models.yaml). Do not set it
# alongside: two settings naming one place drift apart. An empty value is unset.
# ATR_TRAIN_MODELS_CONFIG=

# ── the gateway on idhefix ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two of the three HTTP edges across the seam point here: the promotion gate
# (training/promote.py) and, after the move, eval/. No longer loopback.
ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_URL=http://130.92.59.240:8200
# The gateway reads trained/ at most every ATR_REGISTRY_RELOAD_INTERVAL_S (5 s),
# so the gate's first request after a registration is "404 unknown model". It
# asks again every 10 s for up to 90 s. Keep the spacing above that interval.
# ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_REGISTRY_WAIT_S=90
# ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_REGISTRY_RETRY_S=10
# >>> SHARED <<< — the same key as ATR_API_KEY above.
ATR_TRAIN_GATEWAY_API_KEY=replace-with-a-long-random-shared-secret

# ── the HF hub cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT set here, and that is deliberate: ~/.cache/huggingface/hub is a symlink to
# /mnt/wbkolleg_dh_1/Textrecognition_Training/hf_hub (set 16.09.2026, write test
# passed), shared with the separate lassberg/vlm_training project. Setting
# HF_HOME would route around the symlink and re-download 6.6 TB.
#
# Open question, recorded rather than answered: two *projects* already write that
# cache; two *hosts* is untested. The documented CIFS issue is dedup, explicitly
# "harmless but not optimal" — not concurrency.
# HF_HOME=   <- leave unset

# ── bind and card ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The bind is NOT set here: deploy/systemd/atr-train.service hardcodes
# 127.0.0.1:8204, deliberately. That loopback bind is still the whole security
# model — the service has no authentication of its own — and opening it to
# idhefix without a key is the one change that must not happen alone (#13).
# A .env line could do it quietly; an edit to the unit shows up in git.
#
# The card a job runs on, as a PHYSICAL index (nvidia-smi's numbering). Both A40s
# here are free and NVLinked; per-job allocation is #12.
ATR_TRAIN_GPU=1
